    "created_at": "2025-09-12T15:50:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-12T15:50:05Z",
    "body": "@josepharhar note that it’s not only in `generate implied end tags` where we might expect the algorithm to run. If I’m not misreading the spec, when:\n\n - IN BODY we encounter a star tag whose name is `SELECT`.\n - The parser was not created as part of the fragment case with `SELECT` as context element.\n - The stack of elements has a `SELECT` element in scope.\n\nThen we:\n\n> Pop elements from the stack of open elements until a `select` element has been popped from the stack.\n\nSo I think that this step skips generating implied end tags but might implicitly close any open `OPTION` elements, none of which contain the expected end tag, and one of which might be the selected content.\n\n```html\n<select id=\"real\">\n<option>a\n<option selected>b\n<select id=\"closes-real-but-is-ignored\">\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/3285810179/reactions",
