    "created_at": "2025-09-16T14:04:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-16T14:04:45Z",
    "body": "Handling in generate implied end tags is still not sufficient, because, at least, the end-of-file token doesn't run those steps.\n\nThere are a couple of \"When a foo element is popped off the stack of open elements of an HTML parser or XML parser,\" phrasings:\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#:~:text=The%20element%20is%20popped%20off%20the%20stack%20of%20open%20elements%20of%20an%20HTML%20parser%20or%20XML%20parser%2E\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#:~:text=the%20element%20is%20popped%20off%20the%20stack%20of%20open%20elements%20of%20an%20HTML%20parser%20or%20XML%20parser%2C\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#:~:text=true%2E-,When%20a%20media,false\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#:~:text=When%20a%20textarea%20element%20is%20popped%20off%20the%20stack%20of%20open%20elements%20of%20an%20HTML%20parser%20or%20XML%20parser%2C%20then%20the%20user%20agent%20must%20invoke%20the%20element%27s%20reset%20algorithm%2E\n\nI think that ought to work for `option` as well.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
