    "body": "Thanks @zcorpan! I will make a paragraph like that for option elements for now.\n\n> We should have a follow-up issue on formalizing all those better though, I think. We don't want COMEFROM.\n\nI agree. Would it make sense to move them all into one algorithm that runs any time any element is popped off the stack of open elements? I suppose that it's not perfect unless we also instrument every place that pops elements off the stack of open elements.\n\n> Handling in generate implied end tags is still not sufficient, because, at least, the end-of-file token doesn't run those steps.\n\nDoes this have an explicit step which pops elements off the stack which we could instrument?",
